body:
Hello,

IN condition when settings setMinResult/MaxResults are generating a misformatted query without string value of primary keys being quoted.

(see QueryBuilder.js line 676, sorry for hotfix but no time)
Original code:
```javascript
                                else {
                                    var ids = results.map(function (result) { return result["ids_" + metadata_1.firstPrimaryColumn.propertyName]; });
                                    var areAllNumbers = ids.map(function (id) { return typeof id === "number"; });
                                    if (areAllNumbers) {
                                        // fixes #190. if all numbers then its safe to perform query without parameter
                                        condition = mainAliasName + "." + metadata_1.firstPrimaryColumn.propertyName + " IN (" + ids.join(", ") + ")";
                                    }
                                    else {
                                        parameters["ids"] = ids;
                                        condition = mainAliasName + "." + metadata_1.firstPrimaryColumn.propertyName + " IN (:ids)";
                                    }
                                }
```

Modified code:
```javascript
                                else {
                                    var ids = results.map(function (result) { return result["ids_" + metadata_1.firstPrimaryColumn.propertyName]; });
                                    // HOTFIXED DO NOT UPDATE !!!!
                                    var areAllNumbers = ids.filter(function (id) { return typeof id === "number"; });
                                    if (areAllNumbers.length > 0) {
                                        // fixes #190. if all numbers then its safe to perform query without parameter
                                        condition = mainAliasName + "." + metadata_1.firstPrimaryColumn.propertyName + " IN (" + ids.join(", ") + ")";
                                    }
                                    else {
                                        parameters["ids"] = ids;
                                        condition = mainAliasName + "." + metadata_1.firstPrimaryColumn.propertyName + " IN (:ids)";
                                    }
                                }
```

Explanation: ids.map(.... always interpreted as true because [] == true

Regards.
